IMPORT prelude
IMPORT daydate
IMPORT `roc-core`
IMPORT `roc12-schedule-4-types`
IMPORT `roc12-schedule-4-part-1`
IMPORT `roc12-schedule-4-fees`

-- Rules of Court 2021 (Singapore) -- tests for the Fourth Schedule (court fees): roc12-schedule-4-*.l4.
-- Part A below is written by hand from the figures in the text (lines 7785 to 8826 of the source file) and from the arithmetic the text states.
-- Part B is generated by work/gen_sch4.py and work/gen_sch4_tests.py from the same raw lines: one assertion for each whole-dollar cell, in each column the row has.
-- For a row whose cells number the table's columns, Part B checks that the Part files carry the sum the text prints in the column the text's order gives it.
-- For a row whose columns the generator assigned (the converter lost the column marks; F-S4-A3), the generator's own table fixes the column,
-- so Part B checks the Part file against that table and not against the text; the hand-written tests below check a sample of those columns, including the columns a row does not print.
-- A script that does not read the L4 files made it.

`sch 4 test calendar with a public holiday on 18 March 2025` MEANS `Court calendar` WITH
    `public holidays` IS LIST Date 18 3 2025

`sch 4 test calendar with no public holiday` MEANS `Court calendar` WITH
    `public holidays` IS EMPTY

§ `Part A -- the sums and the arithmetic the text states, written by hand`
-- Arguments of the seam: Part; item; column; units (pages, days, hours); base (an amount); documents; the fee payable for the last application.
-- Item 44: "$2 per page subject to minimum fee of $50 per affidavit" (Supreme Court); "$1 per page subject to a minimum fee of $10 per affidavit" (State Courts).
#ASSERT `sch 4 the fee for this document` 1 "44" `sch 4 column Supreme Court up to $1 million` 10 0 1 0 EQUALS JUST 50 -- 10 pages at $2 is $20, so the $50 minimum
#ASSERT `sch 4 the fee for this document` 1 "44" `sch 4 column Supreme Court up to $1 million` 40 0 1 0 EQUALS JUST 80 -- 40 pages at $2
#ASSERT `sch 4 the fee for this document` 1 "44" `sch 4 column District Court` 5 0 1 0 EQUALS JUST 10 -- 5 pages at $1 is $5, so the $10 minimum
#ASSERT `sch 4 the fee for this document` 1 "44" `sch 4 column Magistrate's Court` 30 0 1 0 EQUALS JUST 30 -- 30 pages at $1
-- Item 40: "6% of amount allowed at assessment of cost subject to a minimum fee of $100" (4% for the Magistrate's Court).
#ASSERT `sch 4 the fee for this document` 1 "40" `sch 4 column Supreme Court up to $1 million` 0 5000 0 0 EQUALS JUST 300 -- 6% of $5,000
#ASSERT `sch 4 the fee for this document` 1 "40" `sch 4 column Supreme Court up to $1 million` 0 1000 0 0 EQUALS JUST 100 -- 6% of $1,000 is $60, so the $100 minimum
#ASSERT `sch 4 the fee for this document` 1 "40" `sch 4 column Magistrate's Court` 0 5000 0 0 EQUALS JUST 200 -- 4% of $5,000
#ASSERT `sch 4 the fee for this document` 1 "40" `sch 4 column Magistrate's Court` 0 2000 0 0 EQUALS JUST 100 -- 4% of $2,000 is $80, so the $100 minimum
-- Item 42: "$50 + 6% of amount of lump sum costs ... subject to a minimum fee of $100" and its sisters.
#ASSERT `sch 4 the fee for this document` 1 "42" `sch 4 column Supreme Court up to $1 million` 0 1000 0 0 EQUALS JUST 110 -- $50 + 6% of $1,000
#ASSERT `sch 4 the fee for this document` 1 "42" `sch 4 column Supreme Court up to $1 million` 0 100 0 0 EQUALS JUST 100 -- $50 + $6 is $56, so the $100 minimum
#ASSERT `sch 4 the fee for this document` 1 "42" `sch 4 column Supreme Court more than $1 million` 0 2000 0 0 EQUALS JUST 220 -- $100 + 6% of $2,000
#ASSERT `sch 4 the fee for this document` 1 "42" `sch 4 column District Court` 0 500 0 0 EQUALS JUST 100 -- $20 + $30 is $50, so the $100 minimum
#ASSERT `sch 4 the fee for this document` 1 "42" `sch 4 column Magistrate's Court` 0 5000 0 0 EQUALS JUST 210 -- $10 + 4% of $5,000
-- Item 7(k)(v): "N + $1,000 where N is the fee payable for the last application" (N + $200 for the State Courts).
#ASSERT `sch 4 the fee for this document` 1 "7(k)(v)" `sch 4 column Supreme Court up to $1 million` 0 0 0 3000 EQUALS JUST 4000 -- N + $1,000
#ASSERT `sch 4 the fee for this document` 1 "7(k)(v)" `sch 4 column District Court` 0 0 0 400 EQUALS JUST 600 -- N + $200
-- Item 10(a): the stepped fee for pages in excess of the limit.
#ASSERT `sch 4 the fee for this document` 1 "10(a)" `sch 4 column Supreme Court up to $1 million` 5 0 1 0 EQUALS JUST 50 -- 5 pages at $10
#ASSERT `sch 4 the fee for this document` 1 "10(a)" `sch 4 column Supreme Court up to $1 million` 10 0 1 0 EQUALS JUST 100 -- the first 10 pages at $10
#ASSERT `sch 4 the fee for this document` 1 "10(a)" `sch 4 column Supreme Court up to $1 million` 15 0 1 0 EQUALS JUST 200 -- 10 at $10 and 5 at $20 (N + $10)
#ASSERT `sch 4 the fee for this document` 1 "10(a)" `sch 4 column Supreme Court up to $1 million` 25 0 1 0 EQUALS JUST 450 -- 10 at $10, 10 at $20 and 5 at $30
#ASSERT `sch 4 the fee for this document` 1 "10(a)" `sch 4 column Supreme Court up to $1 million` 105 0 1 0 EQUALS JUST 6000 -- the rate stops at the $100 maximum: ten tens of pages at $10 to $100, then 5 at $100
#ASSERT `sch 4 the fee for this document` 1 "10(a)" `sch 4 column District Court` 25 0 1 0 EQUALS JUST 225 -- $5 step, $30 maximum: 10 at $5, 10 at $10 and 5 at $15
#ASSERT `sch 4 the fee for this document` 1 "10(a)" `sch 4 column District Court` 65 0 1 0 EQUALS JUST 1200 -- 10 at each of $5 to $30 and then 5 at the $30 maximum
-- Items 49 and 50, 48, 9: sums per document, per page, per party, per day, and a percentage of filing fees.
#ASSERT `sch 4 the fee for this document` 1 "49(a)" `sch 4 column Supreme Court up to $1 million` 10 0 1 0 EQUALS JUST 0 -- draft judgments and requests of an administrative nature: the cell is a dash
#ASSERT `sch 4 the fee for this document` 1 "49(b)" `sch 4 column Supreme Court up to $1 million` 10 0 2 0 EQUALS JUST 14 -- $4 per document plus $0.60 per page: 2 documents, 10 pages
#ASSERT `sch 4 the fee for this document` 1 "49(c)" `sch 4 column Magistrate's Court` 10 0 1 0 EQUALS JUST 12 -- $4 per document plus $0.80 per page
#ASSERT `sch 4 the fee for this document` 1 "50" `sch 4 column District Court` 3 0 0 0 EQUALS JUST 6 -- $2 per document per party served: 3 units (documents served on parties)
#ASSERT `sch 4 the fee for this document` 1 "48" `sch 4 column Supreme Court up to $1 million` 0 500 0 0 EQUALS JUST 80 -- 16% of filing fees of $500
#ASSERT `sch 4 the fee for this document` 1 "9" `sch 4 column Supreme Court up to $1 million` 3 0 0 0 EQUALS JUST 150 -- $50 for each of 3 days
-- Parts 2 to 5, a few sums.
#ASSERT `sch 4 the fee for this document` 3 "4" `sch 4 column Supreme Court up to $1 million` 3 0 2 0 EQUALS JUST 31 -- Part 3 item 4: $8 per document plus $5 per page: 2 documents, 3 pages
#ASSERT `sch 4 the fee for this document` 3 "5" `sch 4 column District Court` 20 0 1 0 EQUALS JUST 8 -- Part 3 item 5: $5 per document plus $0.15 per page
#ASSERT `sch 4 the fee for this document` 3 "7" `sch 4 column Supreme Court up to $1 million` 2 0 0 0 EQUALS JUST 90 -- Part 3 item 7: $45 per page
#ASSERT `sch 4 the fee for this document` 3 "9" `sch 4 column Supreme Court up to $1 million` 1 0 0 0 EQUALS JUST 200 -- Part 3 item 9: $200 per half day
#ASSERT `sch 4 the fee for this document` 3 "9" `sch 4 column Magistrate's Court` 2 0 0 0 EQUALS JUST 200 -- $100 per half day, 2 half days
-- A cell in words only, a column the row does not print, and an item the Schedule does not have.
#ASSERT `sch 4 the fee for this document` 4 "1(b)(iii)" `sch 4 column Supreme Court up to $1 million` 1 0 1 0 EQUALS NOTHING -- Part 4 item 1(b)(iii): which of "$30 for subscribers, $35 for non-subscribers" is charged depends on a fact this seam is not told (see the searcher seam below)
#ASSERT `sch 4 the fee for this document` 1 "16" `sch 4 column District Court` 1 0 1 0 EQUALS NOTHING -- item 16 (Admiralty) prints two cells, which are read as the two Supreme Court columns (F-S4-A3)
#ASSERT `sch 4 the fee for this document` 1 "47" `sch 4 column Supreme Court up to $1 million` 0 1000 0 0 EQUALS NOTHING -- item 47 prints two cells, which are read as the two State Courts columns (F-S4-A3)
#ASSERT `sch 4 the fee for this document` 1 "99" `sch 4 column District Court` 1 0 1 0 EQUALS NOTHING -- no such item
#ASSERT `sch 4 the fee for this document` 6 "1" `sch 4 column District Court` 1 0 1 0 EQUALS NOTHING -- no such Part
#ASSERT `sch 4 the fee for this document` 2 "table 4 item 1" `sch 4 column Supreme Court up to $1 million` 1 0 1 0 EQUALS NOTHING -- Table 4 has a General Division column and no Supreme Court value split
-- The column for the proceedings, and the fee for a document in them.
#ASSERT `sch 4 the column for the proceedings` `Supreme Court` `General Division` 1000000 EQUALS JUST `sch 4 column Supreme Court up to $1 million` -- "With value up to $1 million": exactly $1 million is up to
#ASSERT `sch 4 the column for the proceedings` `Supreme Court` `General Division` 1000001 EQUALS JUST `sch 4 column Supreme Court more than $1 million` -- "With value of more than $1 million"
#ASSERT `sch 4 the column for the proceedings` `State Courts` `District Court` 5 EQUALS JUST `sch 4 column District Court` -- the District Court column
#ASSERT `sch 4 the column for the proceedings` `State Courts` `Magistrate's Court` 5 EQUALS JUST `sch 4 column Magistrate's Court` -- the Magistrate's Court column
#ASSERT `sch 4 the column for the proceedings` `State Courts` `General Division` 5 EQUALS NOTHING -- the General Division is not a State Court
#ASSERT `sch 4 the fee for this document in the proceedings` 1 "1" `Supreme Court` `General Division` 500000 1 0 1 0 EQUALS JUST 500 -- item 1 for a claim of $500,000 in the Supreme Court
#ASSERT `sch 4 the fee for this document in the proceedings` 1 "1" `Supreme Court` `General Division` 2000000 1 0 1 0 EQUALS JUST 1000 -- item 1 for a claim of $2,000,000
#ASSERT `sch 4 the fee for this document in the proceedings` 1 "1" `State Courts` `District Court` 50000 1 0 1 0 EQUALS JUST 150 -- item 1 in the District Court
#ASSERT `sch 4 the fee for this document in the proceedings` 1 "1" `State Courts` `Magistrate's Court` 5000 1 0 1 0 EQUALS JUST 100 -- item 1 in the Magistrate's Court
-- Item 9: the number of court days, whether the fee is payable, and the fee.
#ASSERT `sch 4 part 1 item 9 the number of court days the document remained unfiled` (Date 14 3 2025) (Date 19 3 2025) `sch 4 test calendar with no public holiday` EQUALS 3 -- Sat 15 and Sun 16 are non-court days; Mon 17, Tue 18, Wed 19 are counted
#ASSERT `sch 4 part 1 item 9 the number of court days the document remained unfiled` (Date 14 3 2025) (Date 19 3 2025) `sch 4 test calendar with a public holiday on 18 March 2025` EQUALS 2 -- 18 March is a public holiday
#ASSERT `sch 4 part 1 item 9 the number of court days the document remained unfiled` (Date 14 3 2025) (Date 14 3 2025) `sch 4 test calendar with no public holiday` EQUALS 0 -- filed on the last day
#ASSERT `sch 4 part 1 item 9 the number of court days the document remained unfiled` (Date 14 3 2025) (Date 10 3 2025) `sch 4 test calendar with no public holiday` EQUALS 0 -- filed before the last day
#ASSERT `sch 4 part 1 item 9 the late filing fee is payable` TRUE (Date 14 3 2025) (Date 19 3 2025) EQUALS JUST TRUE -- imposed by the Court and the document remained unfiled after the period
#ASSERT `sch 4 part 1 item 9 the late filing fee is payable` TRUE (Date 14 3 2025) (Date 14 3 2025) EQUALS JUST FALSE -- filed within the period
#ASSERT `sch 4 part 1 item 9 the late filing fee is payable` FALSE (Date 14 3 2025) (Date 19 3 2025) EQUALS JUST FALSE -- "if imposed by the Court"
#ASSERT `sch 4 part 1 item 9 the late filing fee` `sch 4 column Supreme Court up to $1 million` 3 EQUALS JUST 150 -- 3 court days at $50
#ASSERT `sch 4 part 1 item 9 the late filing fee` `sch 4 column Magistrate's Court` 0 EQUALS JUST 0 -- no court day
-- Item 43.  Arguments: column; the fee; the amount that would have been payable under item 40; the fee appears fair and reasonable to the Registrar.
#ASSERT `sch 4 part 1 item 43 the fee is one the Schedule allows` `sch 4 column Supreme Court up to $1 million` 200 5000 TRUE EQUALS JUST TRUE -- the minimum of $200, within the item 40 amount
#ASSERT `sch 4 part 1 item 43 the fee is one the Schedule allows` `sch 4 column Supreme Court up to $1 million` 150 5000 TRUE EQUALS JUST FALSE -- below the $200 minimum
#ASSERT `sch 4 part 1 item 43 the fee is one the Schedule allows` `sch 4 column Supreme Court up to $1 million` 6000 5000 TRUE EQUALS JUST FALSE -- "not exceeding the amount which would have been payable under item 40"
#ASSERT `sch 4 part 1 item 43 the fee is one the Schedule allows` `sch 4 column Supreme Court up to $1 million` 300 5000 FALSE EQUALS JUST FALSE -- "as appears to the Registrar to be fair and reasonable"
#ASSERT `sch 4 part 1 item 43 the fee is one the Schedule allows` `sch 4 column District Court` 100 5000 TRUE EQUALS JUST TRUE -- the $100 minimum of the District Court
#ASSERT `sch 4 part 1 item 43 the fee is one the Schedule allows` `sch 4 column Magistrate's Court` 49 5000 TRUE EQUALS JUST FALSE -- below the $50 minimum of the Magistrate's Court
-- Item 49(2).
#ASSERT `sch 4 part 1 item 49(2) the document is deemed to comprise 2 pages` TRUE EQUALS JUST TRUE -- remotely composed
#ASSERT `sch 4 part 1 item 49(2) the document is deemed to comprise 2 pages` FALSE EQUALS JUST FALSE -- "where the document is remotely composed"
#ASSERT `sch 4 part 1 item 49(2) the number of pages charged for` TRUE 30 EQUALS 2 -- deemed to comprise 2 pages
#ASSERT `sch 4 part 1 item 49(2) the number of pages charged for` FALSE 30 EQUALS 30 -- the pages it has
-- Items 51 to 53.
#ASSERT `sch 4 part 1 items 51 to 53 the column that applies` (Date 31 10 2019) EQUALS `sch 4 column Magistrate's Court` -- lodged before 1 November 2019
#ASSERT `sch 4 part 1 items 51 to 53 the column that applies` (Date 1 11 2019) EQUALS `sch 4 column District Court` -- lodged on 1 November 2019
#ASSERT `sch 4 part 1 items 51 to 53 the column that applies` (Date 1 6 2021) EQUALS `sch 4 column District Court` -- lodged after
-- The introductions to Parts 1, 3, 4 and 5.  Arguments: the fee is of that kind; paid at the time or in the manner the table sets; paid as the Registrar determined.
#ASSERT `sch 4 part 1 the document fee is paid as the Schedule requires` TRUE TRUE FALSE EQUALS JUST TRUE -- paid at the time of filing or sealing
#ASSERT `sch 4 part 1 the document fee is paid as the Schedule requires` TRUE FALSE TRUE EQUALS JUST TRUE -- paid as the Registrar determined
#ASSERT `sch 4 part 1 the document fee is paid as the Schedule requires` TRUE FALSE FALSE EQUALS NOTHING -- QB: a bare "must be paid"
#ASSERT `sch 4 part 1 the document fee is paid as the Schedule requires` FALSE TRUE TRUE EQUALS NOTHING -- not a Part 1 document fee
#ASSERT `sch 4 part 3 the service provision fee is paid as the Schedule requires` TRUE TRUE FALSE EQUALS JUST TRUE -- paid as the table sets out
#ASSERT `sch 4 part 3 the service provision fee is paid as the Schedule requires` TRUE FALSE FALSE EQUALS NOTHING -- QB: a bare "must be paid"
#ASSERT `sch 4 part 4 the search fee is paid as the Schedule requires` TRUE FALSE TRUE EQUALS JUST TRUE -- paid as the Registrar determined
#ASSERT `sch 4 part 4 the search fee is paid as the Schedule requires` TRUE FALSE FALSE EQUALS NOTHING -- QB: a bare "must be paid"
#ASSERT `sch 4 part 5 the Admiralty service provision fee is paid as the Schedule requires` TRUE TRUE FALSE EQUALS JUST TRUE -- paid as the table sets out
#ASSERT `sch 4 part 5 the Admiralty service provision fee is paid as the Schedule requires` TRUE FALSE FALSE EQUALS NOTHING -- QB: a bare "must be paid"
-- Part 2.
#ASSERT `sch 4 part 2 para 1 the Tables specify the fee for the hearing` `sch 4 part 2 para 1(a) a hearing before a District Judge or a Magistrate in open court, including applications fixed on special hearing dates` EQUALS JUST TRUE -- (a)
#ASSERT `sch 4 part 2 para 1 the Tables specify the fee for the hearing` `sch 4 part 2 para 1(e) a hearing before the Registrar in the General Division for the examination of witnesses` EQUALS JUST TRUE -- (e)
#ASSERT `sch 4 part 2 para 1 the Tables specify the fee for the hearing` `sch 4 part 2 para 1 another hearing` EQUALS NOTHING -- not one of (a) to (e)
#ASSERT `sch 4 part 2 para 2 the fee in the Table below is payable for the hearing` TRUE EQUALS JUST TRUE -- a hearing before the Appellate Division or the Court of Appeal
#ASSERT `sch 4 part 2 para 2 the fee in the Table below is payable for the hearing` FALSE EQUALS NOTHING -- another hearing
-- Arguments of each payment function: the fees are paid; the Request is filed in Form 98; that was done at the time the Schedule names.
#ASSERT `sch 4 part 2 table 1 the fees are paid and the Request filed as the Schedule requires` TRUE TRUE TRUE EQUALS JUST TRUE -- all three
#ASSERT `sch 4 part 2 table 1 the fees are paid and the Request filed as the Schedule requires` TRUE FALSE TRUE EQUALS NOTHING -- QB: the Request is not filed
#ASSERT `sch 4 part 2 table 2 the fees are paid and the Request filed as the Schedule requires` TRUE TRUE TRUE EQUALS JUST TRUE -- all three
#ASSERT `sch 4 part 2 table 2 the fees are paid and the Request filed as the Schedule requires` FALSE TRUE TRUE EQUALS NOTHING -- QB: the fees are not paid
#ASSERT `sch 4 part 2 table 3 the fees are paid and the Request filed as the Schedule requires` TRUE TRUE TRUE EQUALS JUST TRUE -- all three
#ASSERT `sch 4 part 2 table 3 the fees are paid and the Request filed as the Schedule requires` TRUE TRUE FALSE EQUALS NOTHING -- QB: not at the time the Schedule names
#ASSERT `sch 4 part 2 table 4 the fees are paid and the Request filed as the Schedule requires` TRUE TRUE TRUE EQUALS JUST TRUE -- all three
#ASSERT `sch 4 part 2 table 4 the fees are paid and the Request filed as the Schedule requires` TRUE TRUE FALSE EQUALS NOTHING -- QB: not at the time the Schedule names
#ASSERT `sch 4 part 2 table 5 the fees are paid and the Request filed as the Schedule requires` TRUE TRUE TRUE EQUALS JUST TRUE -- all three
#ASSERT `sch 4 part 2 table 5 the fees are paid and the Request filed as the Schedule requires` FALSE FALSE FALSE EQUALS NOTHING -- QB: none done
-- Paragraph 2 payment (fix round, item 3): arguments are the fee is paid; the Request is filed in Form 98; the date both were done; and the occasion that fixes the time.
#ASSERT `sch 4 part 2 para 2 the fee is paid and the Request filed as the Schedule requires` TRUE TRUE (Date 10 3 2025) (`sch 4 part 2 para 2 the appellant files his or her Case` (Date 1 3 2025) (Date 15 3 2025)) EQUALS JUST TRUE -- Case filed on 1 March: done on 10 March, inside the 14 days after
#ASSERT `sch 4 part 2 para 2 the fee is paid and the Request filed as the Schedule requires` TRUE TRUE (Date 15 3 2025) (`sch 4 part 2 para 2 the appellant files his or her Case` (Date 1 3 2025) (Date 15 3 2025)) EQUALS JUST TRUE -- the last day of the 14 days
#ASSERT `sch 4 part 2 para 2 the fee is paid and the Request filed as the Schedule requires` TRUE TRUE (Date 1 3 2025) (`sch 4 part 2 para 2 the appellant files his or her Case` (Date 1 3 2025) (Date 15 3 2025)) EQUALS JUST TRUE -- done on the day the Case was filed
#ASSERT `sch 4 part 2 para 2 the fee is paid and the Request filed as the Schedule requires` TRUE TRUE (Date 16 3 2025) (`sch 4 part 2 para 2 the appellant files his or her Case` (Date 1 3 2025) (Date 15 3 2025)) EQUALS JUST FALSE -- one day after the 14 days: outside the period the text fixes ("within 14 days after")
#ASSERT `sch 4 part 2 para 2 the fee is paid and the Request filed as the Schedule requires` TRUE TRUE (Date 28 2 2025) (`sch 4 part 2 para 2 the appellant files his or her Case` (Date 1 3 2025) (Date 15 3 2025)) EQUALS JUST FALSE -- before the Case was filed: not "after" the filing
#ASSERT `sch 4 part 2 para 2 the fee is paid and the Request filed as the Schedule requires` FALSE TRUE (Date 10 3 2025) (`sch 4 part 2 para 2 the appellant files his or her Case` (Date 1 3 2025) (Date 15 3 2025)) EQUALS NOTHING -- QB: the fee is not paid (a bare "must")
#ASSERT `sch 4 part 2 para 2 the fee is paid and the Request filed as the Schedule requires` TRUE FALSE (Date 10 3 2025) (`sch 4 part 2 para 2 the appellant files his or her Case` (Date 1 3 2025) (Date 15 3 2025)) EQUALS NOTHING -- QB: the Request is not filed
#ASSERT `sch 4 part 2 para 2 the fee is paid and the Request filed as the Schedule requires` TRUE TRUE (Date 1 3 2025) (`sch 4 part 2 para 2 the appellant or applicant files the application` (Date 1 3 2025)) EQUALS JUST TRUE -- done at the time the application is filed
#ASSERT `sch 4 part 2 para 2 the fee is paid and the Request filed as the Schedule requires` TRUE TRUE (Date 2 3 2025) (`sch 4 part 2 para 2 the appellant or applicant files the application` (Date 1 3 2025)) EQUALS JUST FALSE -- not at the time the application is filed
#ASSERT `sch 4 part 2 para 2 the fee is paid and the Request filed as the Schedule requires` TRUE TRUE (Date 9 3 2025) (`sch 4 part 2 para 2 a second or subsequent day of hearing is about to begin` (Date 10 3 2025)) EQUALS JUST TRUE -- before the second day of hearing, which begins on 10 March
#ASSERT `sch 4 part 2 para 2 the fee is paid and the Request filed as the Schedule requires` TRUE TRUE (Date 10 3 2025) (`sch 4 part 2 para 2 a second or subsequent day of hearing is about to begin` (Date 10 3 2025)) EQUALS JUST FALSE -- on the day the second day of hearing begins is not before it
#ASSERT `sch 4 part 2 para 2 the fee is paid and the Request filed as the Schedule requires` TRUE TRUE (Date 12 3 2025) (`sch 4 part 2 para 2 a second or subsequent day of hearing is about to begin` (Date 10 3 2025)) EQUALS JUST FALSE -- after the day of hearing began
-- Part 5 items 2 and 3.
#ASSERT `sch 4 part 5 item 2 the commission on the sale` 800 EQUALS 40 -- 5% of the first $1,000
#ASSERT `sch 4 part 5 item 2 the commission on the sale` 1000 EQUALS 50 -- 5% of $1,000
#ASSERT `sch 4 part 5 item 2 the commission on the sale` 3000 EQUALS 100 -- $50 and 2.5% of the $2,000 above $1,000
#ASSERT `sch 4 part 5 item 2 the commission on the sale` 0 EQUALS 0 -- nothing sold
#ASSERT `sch 4 part 5 item 3 the commission on the release of a ship` (JUST 1000) 2000 2 EQUALS 1200 -- ($500 + 10 cents x 1,000 net registered tons) x 2 months
#ASSERT `sch 4 part 5 item 3 the commission on the release of a ship` NOTHING 2000 1 EQUALS 700 -- net tonnage not ascertained: gross tonnage 2,000, one month
-- Fix round, item 2: fees charged by a count.  The count is the units argument.  Each row is tried at a count of 0 (owes nothing), 1 and more than 1 in its first column, and at more than 1 in the others.
#ASSERT `sch 4 the fee for this document` 1 "13" `sch 4 column Supreme Court up to $1 million` 0 0 1 0 EQUALS JUST 0 -- Part 1 item 13: $50 a witness (count 0)
#ASSERT `sch 4 the fee for this document` 1 "13" `sch 4 column Supreme Court up to $1 million` 1 0 1 0 EQUALS JUST 50 -- Part 1 item 13: $50 a witness (count 1)
#ASSERT `sch 4 the fee for this document` 1 "13" `sch 4 column Supreme Court up to $1 million` 3 0 1 0 EQUALS JUST 150 -- Part 1 item 13: $50 a witness (count 3)
#ASSERT `sch 4 the fee for this document` 1 "13" `sch 4 column Supreme Court more than $1 million` 3 0 1 0 EQUALS JUST 300 -- Part 1 item 13: 3 units at $100
#ASSERT `sch 4 the fee for this document` 1 "13" `sch 4 column District Court` 3 0 1 0 EQUALS JUST 30 -- Part 1 item 13: 3 units at $10
#ASSERT `sch 4 the fee for this document` 1 "13" `sch 4 column Magistrate's Court` 3 0 1 0 EQUALS JUST 30 -- Part 1 item 13: 3 units at $10
#ASSERT `sch 4 the fee for this document` 1 "14" `sch 4 column Supreme Court up to $1 million` 0 0 1 0 EQUALS JUST 0 -- Part 1 item 14: $100 a witness (count 0)
#ASSERT `sch 4 the fee for this document` 1 "14" `sch 4 column Supreme Court up to $1 million` 1 0 1 0 EQUALS JUST 100 -- Part 1 item 14: $100 a witness (count 1)
#ASSERT `sch 4 the fee for this document` 1 "14" `sch 4 column Supreme Court up to $1 million` 3 0 1 0 EQUALS JUST 300 -- Part 1 item 14: $100 a witness (count 3)
#ASSERT `sch 4 the fee for this document` 1 "14" `sch 4 column Supreme Court more than $1 million` 3 0 1 0 EQUALS JUST 600 -- Part 1 item 14: 3 units at $200
#ASSERT `sch 4 the fee for this document` 1 "14" `sch 4 column District Court` 3 0 1 0 EQUALS JUST 60 -- Part 1 item 14: 3 units at $20
#ASSERT `sch 4 the fee for this document` 1 "14" `sch 4 column Magistrate's Court` 3 0 1 0 EQUALS JUST 60 -- Part 1 item 14: 3 units at $20
#ASSERT `sch 4 the fee for this document` 1 "5" `sch 4 column Supreme Court up to $1 million` 0 0 1 0 EQUALS JUST 0 -- Part 1 item 5: $100 a party (count 0)
#ASSERT `sch 4 the fee for this document` 1 "5" `sch 4 column Supreme Court up to $1 million` 1 0 1 0 EQUALS JUST 100 -- Part 1 item 5: $100 a party (count 1)
#ASSERT `sch 4 the fee for this document` 1 "5" `sch 4 column Supreme Court up to $1 million` 3 0 1 0 EQUALS JUST 300 -- Part 1 item 5: $100 a party (count 3)
#ASSERT `sch 4 the fee for this document` 1 "5" `sch 4 column Supreme Court more than $1 million` 3 0 1 0 EQUALS JUST 600 -- Part 1 item 5: 3 units at $200
#ASSERT `sch 4 the fee for this document` 1 "5" `sch 4 column District Court` 3 0 1 0 EQUALS JUST 60 -- Part 1 item 5: 3 units at $20
#ASSERT `sch 4 the fee for this document` 1 "5" `sch 4 column Magistrate's Court` 3 0 1 0 EQUALS JUST 30 -- Part 1 item 5: 3 units at $10
#ASSERT `sch 4 the fee for this document` 2 "table 2 item 2" `sch 4 column District Court` 0 0 1 0 EQUALS JUST 0 -- Part 2 item table 2 item 2: $100 a hour or part of an hour (count 0)
#ASSERT `sch 4 the fee for this document` 2 "table 2 item 2" `sch 4 column District Court` 1 0 1 0 EQUALS JUST 100 -- Part 2 item table 2 item 2: $100 a hour or part of an hour (count 1)
#ASSERT `sch 4 the fee for this document` 2 "table 2 item 2" `sch 4 column District Court` 3 0 1 0 EQUALS JUST 300 -- Part 2 item table 2 item 2: $100 a hour or part of an hour (count 3)
#ASSERT `sch 4 the fee for this document` 2 "table 2 item 2" `sch 4 column Magistrate's Court` 3 0 1 0 EQUALS JUST 150 -- Part 2 item table 2 item 2: 3 units at $50
#ASSERT `sch 4 the fee for this document` 2 "table 5 item 2" `sch 4 column Supreme Court up to $1 million` 0 0 1 0 EQUALS JUST 0 -- Part 2 item table 5 item 2: $250 a hour or part of an hour (count 0)
#ASSERT `sch 4 the fee for this document` 2 "table 5 item 2" `sch 4 column Supreme Court up to $1 million` 1 0 1 0 EQUALS JUST 250 -- Part 2 item table 5 item 2: $250 a hour or part of an hour (count 1)
#ASSERT `sch 4 the fee for this document` 2 "table 5 item 2" `sch 4 column Supreme Court up to $1 million` 3 0 1 0 EQUALS JUST 750 -- Part 2 item table 5 item 2: $250 a hour or part of an hour (count 3)
#ASSERT `sch 4 the fee for this document` 2 "table 5 item 2" `sch 4 column Supreme Court more than $1 million` 3 0 1 0 EQUALS JUST 1500 -- Part 2 item table 5 item 2: 3 units at $500
#ASSERT `sch 4 the fee for this document` 3 "10" `sch 4 column Supreme Court up to $1 million` 0 0 1 0 EQUALS JUST 0 -- Part 3 item 10: $25 a person making the affidavit (count 0)
#ASSERT `sch 4 the fee for this document` 3 "10" `sch 4 column Supreme Court up to $1 million` 1 0 1 0 EQUALS JUST 25 -- Part 3 item 10: $25 a person making the affidavit (count 1)
#ASSERT `sch 4 the fee for this document` 3 "10" `sch 4 column Supreme Court up to $1 million` 3 0 1 0 EQUALS JUST 75 -- Part 3 item 10: $25 a person making the affidavit (count 3)
#ASSERT `sch 4 the fee for this document` 3 "10" `sch 4 column Supreme Court more than $1 million` 3 0 1 0 EQUALS JUST 75 -- Part 3 item 10: 3 units at $25
