#ASSERT `sch 4 the stated fee is the fee charged` 2 "table 1 item 1" `sch 4 column District Court` 1 0 1 0 500 EQUALS JUST FALSE -- Table 1: $500 is the fee for each day after the first, and a one-day hearing has none
#ASSERT `sch 4 the stated fee is the fee charged` 2 "table 1 item 1" `sch 4 column District Court` 3 0 1 0 1000 EQUALS JUST TRUE -- Table 1: days 2 and 3 at $500
#ASSERT `sch 4 the stated fee is the fee charged` 2 "appellate item 1" `sch 4 column Supreme Court more than $1 million` 2 0 1 0 6000 EQUALS JUST TRUE -- para 2: the second day at $6,000
#ASSERT `sch 4 the stated fee is the fee charged` 2 "table 3 item 1" `sch 4 column Supreme Court up to $1 million` 3 0 1 0 0 EQUALS JUST TRUE -- Table 3: a three-day hearing owes nothing for the fourth day
#ASSERT `sch 4 the stated fee is the fee charged` 1 "43" `sch 4 column Supreme Court up to $1 million` 1 0 1 0 200 EQUALS NOTHING -- item 43: the Schedule prints no sum, so no stated sum is said to be the fee (see the minimum function)
